Batch C (tasks 5–6) and Batch D (tasks 7–8) are done and marked `[x]` in `tasks.md`. `npm test` passes with 284 tests in 25 files (270 and 23 after Batch C), and `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean.

1. **Hook:** `decideHook` and `runHookCommand` are in `src/cli/hook-command.ts`, and `main.ts` now dispatches `hook`. There are 11 unit and property tests covering every event you listed, plus `str_replace` first/all/no-match and whitespace-only churn.
2. **Latency:** the naive path took about 27,000 ms for 1,500 tombstones and a 300-line write, so I added the exact prefilter in `src/core/watch.ts`. That brings it to **7–15 ms**, depending on the run. A property test checks that prefilter on and off give equal hits, with comment lines and two threshold sets. A write containing a block-comment opener (`/*`, `<!--`, `{-`) turns the prefilter off. It takes about **475 ms** (window indexing only), so it misses the 200 ms budget. I reported it in `tasks.md` and did not cap it.
3. **MCP:** `src/mcp/tools.ts` holds the pure handlers (14 tests including the limit property) and `src/mcp/server.ts` wires the three tools over stdio. The server test spawns the built `dist/mcp/server.js` and calls all three tools through the SDK client. It also covers the missing-graveyard error and checks that stdout carries only JSON-RPC frames.
4. **Dependencies:** `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` and `zod` are added to `package.json` and the lockfile. I did not commit; the changes are in the working tree.
